  <content>
  <section id="sect-00001"><para id="para-00001">In this lesson, you will begin to understand what makes a sequence a geometric sequence and how that connects to exponential functions. Using graphs, you will explore how growing and shrinking patterns represent geometric sequences.</para>
<para id="para-00002">When you finish this lesson, you will be able to:</para>
<list id="list-00001">
  <item>
    Find missing terms in a geometric sequence.
 </item>
</list>
<para id="para-00003">Here are the <emphasis>activities</emphasis> that will help you reach those goals:</para>
<list id="list-00002">
  <item>
    4.15.1: What Are the Patterns?
 </item>
  <item>
    4.15.2: Using Tables and Graphs to Represent Geometric Sequences <list id="list-00003">
    <item>
      4.15.2: Self Check
   </item>
    <item>
      4.15.2: Additional Resources
   </item>
  </list>
 </item>
 
  <item>
    4.15.3: Complete the Sequence <list id="list-00004">
    <item>
      4.15.3: Self Check
   </item>
    <item>
      4.15.3: Additional Resources
   </item>
  </list>
 </item>
 
  <item>
    4.15.4: Connecting the Common Ratio and the Term in a Sequence
 </item>
</list>
<para id="para-00004">After that, you’ll <emphasis>practice and review</emphasis>.</para>
<list id="list-00005">
  <item>
    4.15.5: Practice
 </item>
  <item>
    4.15.6: Lesson Summary
 </item>
</list></section>
